<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego Luis de San Vitores</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1627">1627</a>–<a href="/years/1672">1672</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diego Luis de San Vitores was a Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> missionary who founded the first permanent Catholic mission in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariana-islands">Mariana Islands</a>, landing on Guam in 1668. He named the islands after Queen Mariana of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and began the Spanish colonisation of Guam. He was killed by a Chamorro chief in 1672, his death was followed by decades of war, and he was beatified in 1985.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-luis-de-san-vitores.jpg" alt="Diego Luis de San Vitores" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Rizi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Juan_rizi-fray_alonso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
